# tools/al/ales_stereo_infinite_clip_witness.rish — stereo_infinite_clip: the infinite clipper carried into stereo with ONE SHARED RAIL, both channels in lockstep, CLOSING the dead-zone family in stereo (ALES143).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES143.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-043212_fill-ales143-lotus-stereo-infinite-clip.md
# Stands on: lotus/infinite_clip.rye (ALES89 — the mono infinite clipper run once per channel, y = if |x| ≤ t then 0 else sign(x)·sample_max with no rail edge), lotus/stereo_center_clip.rye (ALES141 — the hard sibling
# whose dead zone this shares, the same samples silenced and the survivors pinned to the rail instead of passed), lotus/pan.rye (ALES10 — the StereoClip, two mono Clips left/right, and its balance invariant),
# lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip, its buf/len/samples, sample_min/max). A Lotus master is a StereoClip whose defining invariant is that left and right hold the same length. This rung carries ALES89's rail into
# stereo — silencing the quiet middle and pinning every survivor to plus or minus sample_max in both channels, a sine becoming a square, one rail landing on both speakers together. It is the third and loudest reading
# of the survivor's fate (the hard center clip passes, the soft shifts, the infinite clip pins), closing the dead-zone family in stereo. It is odd, so it holds the inter-channel antisymmetry (an out-of-phase master
# staying out of phase), yet it collapses the inter-channel ratio to unity (every survivor slammed to the same magnitude), and thresh zero is the pure comparator rather than the identity.
#
# lotus/stereo_infinite_clip.rye validates both channels once against the shared threshold and length before either is mutated (BadThreshold on a threshold outside [0, sample_max], BadRange on a span outside the
# samples), then infinite-clips both channels through ALES89's infinite_clip; InfiniteClipError reused whole. The crux is four laws. THE STEREO INFINITE-CLIP LAW: each channel equals ALES89's mono infinite_clip with
# the same threshold byte for byte. THE BALANCE / LENGTH LAW: left.len == right.len after, both holding their starting length. THE PER-CHANNEL ODD / RAIL LAW: the antisymmetry held, the ratio collapsed to unity, an
# identical-channel master staying identical, thresh zero the pure comparator, the map idempotent below the rail, the same dead zone as ALES141. THE ATOMICITY / DEGENERATE LAW: a refusal leaves both channels untouched
# and balanced, count zero the identity.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_stereo_infinite_clip_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-infinite-clip: Language EN — stereo_infinite_clip infinite-clips a span in both channels of a stereo master with the same threshold, silencing every sample whose magnitude is at most the threshold and pinning every louder sample to plus or minus sample_max, the same rail on each, so one infinite clip lands on both speakers together. A Lotus master is two Clips heard together, one per speaker, whose defining invariant is that left and right hold the same length so the two channels stay aligned in time. This rung closes the dead-zone family in stereo on ALES89's infinite clipper, running the proven mono infinite clip on each channel with the same threshold, validated once against the shared threshold and length before either channel is mutated so a refusal never infinite-clips one channel and leaves the other whole."
say "ales-stereo-infinite-clip: Style Radiant — the two center clips read one axis, the survivor's fate, two ways: the hard center clip passes the survivor at its own value, the soft center clip shifts it toward zero by the threshold. This rung reads that axis its third and loudest way: it pins every survivor all the way to the rail, discarding every trace of amplitude and keeping only the sign, so a sine in becomes a square out, the harshest fuzz there is, the comparator of every zero-crossing detector. The infinite clip is odd, because the sign flips with the sign and the negative survivor pins to minus sample_max rather than sample_min precisely to keep the map exactly odd for every i16 including the deepest sample, so like both center clips it holds the inter-channel antisymmetry: an out-of-phase master, right the exact negation of left, comes back still out of phase. Yet it is the extreme of the family, because every survivor is slammed to the same magnitude regardless of its input, so a shared rail collapses the inter-channel ratio to unity: a one-to-two master comes back one-to-one where both survive. And thresh zero is not the identity here, as it was for the two center clips, but the pure comparator: every nonzero sample pins to the rail and only exact silence survives as zero. Idempotence holds precisely below the rail, on zero through sample_max minus one, because a pinned survivor at sample_max clears any threshold below the rail. The rule is stated positively: the infinite clip is exact for every i16 with no rail edge and no saturate, only minus sample_max, zero, or sample_max ever written; it carries one parameter, the threshold magnitude, and names two faults. Refuse BadThreshold on a threshold outside zero through sample_max and BadRange on a span outside the samples, each before either channel is mutated, else infinite-clip both channels over the span with the same threshold via ALES89's infinite clip. It reuses ALES89's InfiniteClipError by name and ALES89's infinite clip for the arithmetic, inventing no new fault and no new primitive. All three dead-zone members silence the same dead zone, proven against ALES141. The crux stands out as four laws: the stereo infinite-clip law, the balance / length law, the per-channel odd / rail law (the antisymmetry held, the ratio collapsed to unity, an identical-channel master staying identical, thresh zero the pure comparator, the map idempotent below the rail), and the atomicity / degenerate law (any refusal leaves both channels byte for byte untouched and still balanced, count zero the identity on both)."
say "ales-stereo-infinite-clip: Lens TAME — two bounded i16 Clips (left, right) infinite-clipped in lockstep by one shared rail; the balance invariant is asserted on entry and exit, the threshold and span are bound-checked once before any write, and because those checks hold identically for both channels each mono infinite clip is pre-validated to succeed so no refusal can land between the two channel edits; infinite_clip walks the span once per channel, taking each magnitude in i32 so the magnitude of sample_min is representable and pinning each survivor to one of two signed constants with its sign held, the output one of three legal i16 values by construction so there is no rail edge and no saturate, never touching a byte past len so the length holds exactly; it reuses ALES89's infinite clip per channel over its public API and ALES89's InfiniteClipError whole, inventing no new primitive; the stereo infinite-clip law is proven against ALES89's own infinite clip run per channel, the per-channel odd / rail law proves the out-of-phase field's antisymmetry is held while the one-to-two field's ratio collapses to unity, that thresh zero is the pure comparator and the map idempotent below the rail, and the family bond against ALES141's stereo center clip shows the same dead zone silenced, the two refusals leave both channels byte-for-byte untouched, and count zero is the identity; siloed to lotus/, no real sample rate, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_infinite_clip"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_infinite_clip.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-infinite-clip: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_infinite_clip.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-infinite-clip: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-infinite-clip: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-infinite-clip' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-infinite-clip: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-infinite-clip line"
